** Session 3: Daggers in the Dark **


   I'm now entering the Caverns area. I breathe a slight sigh of
relief. This level is lit. I have the Light spell, but I want to save
my power for Force Bolt. I still don't have any daggers, and would
rather kill things at a distance. Although the quarterstaff is blessed
and +1, it's really not Elryk's style... (Patience. But I can't wait
to get "Stormbringer" from Anhur...)

   Misericorde and I are almost immediately beset upon by the
denizens, of course, and as expected. By this time, she has grown up
pretty good, and gets in quite a few attacks per round, compared to
Elryk. As long as my character has a clear line of fire at approaching
monsters, I feel confident enough to handle some dumb dwarfs and,
goofy gnomes. Then; soon enough...

<The spell hits the gnome lord! You kill the gnome lord! Welcome to
experience level 4. You feel awake! Splat! >

Elryk the Conjurer  St:10 Dx:16 Co:16 In:18 Wi:8 Ch:8  Chaotic
Dlvl:5  $:0  HP:32(32)  Pw:38(46)  AC:6  Exp:4  T:1496

   I'm starting to notice that I'm getting odd messages (such as the
one above). 'You feel awake'? There wasn't a sleep trap, nor did the
monster throw a potion of sleep at me. Besides; I'm an elf. Elves are
resistant to sleep. And what's with the 'splat'? I don't see any
Keystone Kops around? I shrug it off for now...

   The status above shows Dlvl:5, but this was in the Caverns area.
And, look at how many hit points and power points I now have. This is
great!

   Shortly after these immediate battles; I acquired 4 daggers. I now
have chucking weaponry! <big grin>

   Shortly after that: I found that I couldn't hit the broad side of a
dwarf (or anything else) when I threw them. <grimace>

   So; Force Bolt had to be relied upon as my "fail safe", yet again.
This was especially so, whenever a gnome lord appeared. They're always
dangerous, due to the wands they've often been known to carry.

   After I had cleared quite a large area of this level, I was going
around, picking up my daggers, when a throng of hill orcs came along.
Elryk's eyes narrowed in anticipation. These guys will serve well as
dagger chucking targets!

   I took a step forward, towards them. Then, immediately; fell in a
poison spiked pit!

   Awww... <groan>

   Damn. Strength took a big hit. <concern>

   It took me forever to crawl out of it. All the while, I kept on
hearing noises in the distance. When, I finally managed to extricate
myself, there were only two hill orcs left!

   Quickly, before Misericorde kills them all; I lined up one of them
and threw a dagger...

   It traveled three (maybe four, but I can almost swear it was three)
squares and fell to the floor!

   <hang head> I suppose my reduced strength will hamper the rate at
which I can increase my daggers skill... <sad face>

   Charge! (With a dagger wielded.)

< You kill the hill orc! Welcome to experience level 5. >

Elryk the Conjurer  St:7 Dx:16 Co:16 In:18 Wi:8 Ch:8  Chaotic
Dlvl:5  $:13  HP:28(42)  Pw:52(52)  AC:6  Exp:5  T:1710

   With my new strength, I found out that I couldn't carry too much
booty before finding myself burdened. This made clearing the level
quite a process, in terms of time. I'm very meticulous concerning a
"clean dungeon" approach, and game strategy. Everything has to be in
its place, and unless pressed for some reason or other, I leave no
stone (or boulder) unturned.

   Eventually...

< You destroy the human zombie!  Welcome to experience level 6. >

Elryk the Thaumaturge  St:7 Dx:16 Co:16 In:18 Wi:8 Ch:8  Chaotic
Dlvl:5  $:0  HP:49(49)  Pw:62(66)  AC:6  Exp:6  T:2040

   Around this point, my little kitten which is now a large cat,
fights like a lion!

   Caverns level 6 was dark.

   Oh great. <roll eyes> I'll be trying to practice my dagger chucking
- at the stand off distance of three - with the killer strength of
seven - in the dark, eh? Let's see how this goes... <stick out tongue>

   Many, countless and futile, attempts at trying to hit something
later; I was forced - yet again - to fall back upon the ol' Force Bolt
spell...

< The spell hits the pony! You kill the pony! Welcome to experience
level 7. Misericorde picks up a wand. >

Elryk the Thaumaturge  St:7 Dx:16 Co:16 In:18 Wi:8 Ch:8  Chaotic
Dlvl:6  $:0  HP:23(57)  Pw:49(82)  AC:6  Exp:7  T:2616

   By now; I was starting to get used to having the strength of a
kobold. It was strangely familiar to the real Elric (by Micheal
Moorcocke), who was plagued with sickness. So I didn't let it bother
me no more. In fact I kind of liked it (!). Gave it all more of a role
playing feel to the game. <smile>

   I found the following message kind of odd...

< The spell hits the large dog! The spell hits the lizard! The lizard
resists! You kill the lizard! >

T:3081

   Resisting something, then getting killed by that same something, is
definitely weird - I find any way. And lizards can resist spells?
Never remembered seeing something like that before (?). (Later on, in
other sessions, you'll see that I came across something similar to
this, many times.)

   Caverns level 7 was immediately familiar from the first room
entered. Actually; being a room upon descending, instead of a cavern,
was what gave it away. <wink>

   I've found Temple Town.

   In the passageway leading from the room with the stairs; I killed a
rat (stabbed it to death), and got the message that I'd been patiently
waiting for to appear. Went to the enhancement screen, then checked a
box...

< You are now more skilled in dagger. >  

T: 3093

   Finally! <roll eyes>

   That was the reason why I was playing so long this time (!).

   Boy. Am I ever lucky that I have so much power. Else; my strategy
of depending on dagger chucking to get me through the beginning of the
game - sure don't look too good right now! <laugh!>

   I save the game, and go for a well deserved nights' rest.

